{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":10000,"url":"https://thediplomat.com/2023/10/02/indonesia-launches-high-speed-rail/"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://thediplomat.com/2023/10/02/indonesia-launches-high-speed-rail/:\n### Archive\n\n## October 2, 2023\n\n[![Ajai Sahni on Canada and the Khalistani Movement](https://thediplomat.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/sizes/thumbnail/thediplomat_2023-09-30-013243.jpg \"Ajai Sahni on Canada and the Khalistani Movement\")\n\n#### Ajai Sahni on Canada and the Khalistani Movement\n\n###### By Sudha Ramachandran\n\n“The present ‘movement’ is diaspora-led, fed by the ISI and implicitly supported by some countries, most prominently Canada, for geostrategic reasons and domestic political imperatives.”](/2023/10/ajai-sahni-on-canada-and-the-khalistani-movement/)[![Germany Hosts Central Asian Leaders for Summit](https://thediplomat.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/sizes/thumbnail/thediplomat_2023-10-02-143039.jpg \"Germany Hosts Central Asian Leaders for Summit\")\n\n#### Germany Hosts Central Asian Leaders for Summit\n\n###### By Catherine Putz\n\nAttending yet another summit, it’s clear that diplomatic outreach to Central Asia is in high gear across the West.](/2023/10/germany-hosts-central-asian-leaders-for-summit/)[![The State of China’s Semiconductor Industry](https://thediplomat.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/sizes/thumbnail/thediplomat_2021-09-07-7.jpg \"The State of China’s Semiconductor Industry\")\n\n#### The State of China’s Semiconductor Industry\n\n###### By Mercy A. Kuo\n\nInsights from Douglas Fuller.](/2023/10/the-state-of-chinas-semiconductor-industry/)[![Even Before the Latest Bombing, Mastung Was a Hotbed for Violent Insurgency](https://thediplomat.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/sizes/thumbnail/thediplomat-2021-05-20-4.jpg \"Even Before the Latest Bombing, Mastung Was a Hotbed for Violent Insurgency\")\n\n#### Even Before the Latest Bombing, Mastung Was a Hotbed for Violent Insurgency\n\n###### By Kiyya Baloch\n\nThere is a widespread belief in Balochistan that the authorities in Pakistan have deliberately allowed Islamic fundamentalism to flourish in the province in general – and in Mastung in particular.](/2023/10/even-before-the-latest-bombing-mastung-was-a-hotbed-for-violent-insurgency/)[![South Korea: America’s Forgotten Ally? ](https://thediplomat.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/sizes/thumbnail/thediplomat_2023-05-01-130340.jpg \"South Korea: America’s Forgotten Ally? \")\n\n#### South Korea: America’s Forgotten Ally?\n\n###### By Troy Stangarone and Clint Work\n\nSouth Korea’s reluctance to play a more vocal role often leaves its sizable contributions less noticed than those of other allies.](/2023/10/south-korea-americas-forgotten-ally/)[![East Asian Tensions and the Lessons From Hanoi](https://thediplomat.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/sizes/thumbnail/thediplomat_2023-10-02-132707.jpg \"East Asian Tensions and the Lessons From Hanoi\")\n\n#### East Asian Tensions and the Lessons From Hanoi\n\n###### By ISOZAKI Atsuhito\n\nVietnamese diplomacy offers some useful reminders for key actors in a troubled region.](/2023/10/east-asian-tensions-and-the-lessons-from-hanoi/)[![Can Sri Lanka Afford to Go Green?](https://thediplomat.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/sizes/thumbnail/thediplomat_2023-10-02-124249.jpg \"Can Sri Lanka Afford to Go Green?\")\n\n#### Can Sri Lanka Afford to Go Green?\n\n###### By Michael Iveson\n\nSri Lanka will not fulfill its renewable energy commitments under current economic conditions. But what if the government could simultaneously tackle its climate, energy, and debt crises?](/2023/10/can-sri-lanka-afford-to-go-green/)[![Pakistan’s Outdated Counter&shy;terrorism Framework Requires Major Revamp](https://thediplomat.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/sizes/thumbnail/thediplomat_2023-10-02-030431.png \"Pakistan’s Outdated Counter&shy;terrorism Framework Requires Major Revamp\")\n\n#### Pakistan’s Outdated Counter­terrorism Framework Requires Major Revamp\n\n###### By Abdul Basit\n\nTalks with the TTP, for example, allowed some factions to return to Pakistan and gain legitimacy as well.](/2023/10/pakistans-outdated-counterterrorism-framework-requires-major-revamp/)[![Hasina, Macron Seal Deal on Aircraft that Bangladesh Doesn’t Need, Cannot Afford](https://thediplomat.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/sizes/thumbnail/thediplomat_2023-10-01-115453.jpeg \"Hasina, Macron Seal Deal on Aircraft that Bangladesh Doesn’t Need, Cannot Afford\")\n\n#### Hasina, Macron Seal Deal on Aircraft that Bangladesh Doesn’t Need, Cannot Afford\n\n###### By Zia Hassan\n\nThe French PM secured a lucrative contract for Airbus. In return, his lips will remain sealed on a likely undemocratic election.](/2023/10/hasina-macron-seal-deal-on-aircraft-that-bangladesh-doesnt-need-cannot-afford/)"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
