ssistance disbursement), R-6B-S2 (KUR), N-6B-1 (BRIN presidential-decree founding and \"Jokowi himself also seemed to have lost interest\"). Other items are institutional, subnational, or inherited patterns.\n\n**Search limitation note (round 1):** A targeted search for 2023-distinct national human-development indicators (BPS stunting prevalence, BPS poverty line, BKKBN stunting data) was attempted but the BPS press-release URLs surfaced in 2026 or returned 404. The 2023 BPS March poverty rate (9.36%) is cited by EAF (Jan 2024) but not surfaced as an independent BPS primary source in this worker session. The EAF macro-outcome statement about 2023 GDP/inflation is the strongest 2023-distinct outcome anchor available.\n\n---\n\n### CHAPTER 7B — Ruler Personal Integrity and Honesty\n\n**Round-0 estimate:** 5 defensible / 6 families. Reviewer issues: ministerial corruption attributed to Jokowi without personal-conduct evidence; broad structural/retrospective items not fitted to 2023; under-specified accountability chain.\n\n**Round-1 changes:** Re-type items that lack personal-conduct attribution. Add a direct, attributable item on the Firli appointment (2019) and dismissal (Nov 2023). Add a counter-claim (N-7B-6) on Jokowi's January 2023 admission without apology. Split bundled pattern items into per-claim units.\n\n#### 7B retained/restructured items\n\n| ID | Claim | URL / locator | Source type & conf. | Period fit | Ruler attribution evidence | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **R-7B-I1** | BBC News (23 Nov 2023): \"Police said there was enough evidence to link Firli Bahuri, chairman of the Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK), to corruption at the country's ministry of agriculture… 'a state official extorted money at the agriculture ministry from 2020 to 2023.'… officers said they had uncovered foreign exchange transaction documents and US dollars worth 7.4bn Indonesian Rupiah ($477,730)… President Joko Widodo said on Thursday he would 'respect the process of law.'\" | https://www.bbc.com/news/world-67509472 | Major public-service media · medium_high | Target-year (Nov 2023) | **Direct** — Jokowi's own statement \"respect the process of law\" is on record. The accountability response is documented. | `final_evidence` |\n| **S-7B-I2a** *(split)* | The Jakarta Post (23 Nov 2023): \"Firli was named the KPK chief in 2019, around the same time critics said changes to the law governing the agency had weakened it, triggering a series of 'save the KPK' protests.\" Establishes the appointment as a Jokowi decision. | https://www.thejakartapost.com/indonesia/2023/11/23/police-name-kpk-chief-firli-as-suspect-in-alleged-extortion.html | Reputable national media · medium_high | Cross-period (appointment 2019, suspect status 2023) | **Direct** — appointment is a Jokowi decision; the 2019 KPK-weakening law was a Jokowi-era reform. | `final_evidence` |\n| **S-7B-I2b** *(split)* | The Jakarta Post (23 Nov 2023): \"Former agriculture minister Limpo resigned in October because of the allegations levelled at him. He is the **sixth minister to be investigated for corruption since President Joko 'Jokowi' Widodo took office in 2014**.\" Establishes the pattern across Jokowi's tenure. | Same URL | Reputable national media · medium_high | Cross-period (covers 2023) | **Direct** — pattern claim attributed to Jokowi's cabinet. | `final_evidence` |\n| **N-7B-1** | Asia News Network (28 Nov 2023): \"Jokowi dismisses Firli, names interim KPK chief.\" Establishes the dismissal as a direct Jokowi action in 2023. | https://asianews.network/jokowi-dismisses-firli-names-interim-kpk-chief/ | Reputable regional media · medium_high | Target-year (Nov 2023) | **Direct** — dismissal is a Jokowi action. | `final_evidence` |\n| **N-7B-2** | BBC News (23 Nov 2023): \"The president must temporarily suspend any KPK chief named as a criminal suspect, according to Indonesian law.\" Establishes the legal frame for the dismissal (rule of law applied). | https://www.bbc.com/news/world-67509472 | Major public-service media · medium_high | Target-year | **Direct** — Jokowi followed the legal frame. | `final_evidence` |\n| **R-7B-I4** *(re-typed)* | Freedom House 2024: \"In 2022, human rights activists Haris Azhar and Fatia Maulidiyanti were formally charged with defaming a government minister under the UU ITE… The trial began in April 2023 and was ongoing at year's end.\" | https://freedomhouse.org/country/indonesia/freedom-world/2024, section E2 | NGO · medium_high | Target-year (trial April 2023) | **Ministerial complaint** (Luhut). No evidence of Jokowi's personal direction. Re-typed to `context` for ruler-attribution; retained as `final_evidence` for institutional chapter (4B). | `context` (7B); `final_evidence` (4B) |\n| **R-7B-I5** | Freedom House 2024: UU ITE amendments passed by DPR in December 2023; \"the amended UU ITE also prohibits expression that fosters 'feelings of hatred or hostility' for protected individuals. The amended law was not signed by the president by year's end.\" | https://freedomhouse.org/country/indonesia/freedom-world/2024, section D4 | NGO · medium_high | Target-year (Dec 2023) | **Direct** — non-signature is a Jokowi action. | `final_evidence` |\n| **S-7B-I6a** *(split, re-typed)* | BTI 2026 Indonesia, §2.4: \"the revision of the laws governing the working of the Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK) had a similar goal [to Job Creation Laws]. They originated from the need to make bureaucrats feel more secure in implementing government projects given that a very large number of bureaucrats had earlier been prosecuted by the KPK for alleged corruption.\" | https://bti-project.org/en/reports/country-report/IDN, §2.4 | Academic index · medium_high | Cross-period (covers 2023 conduct) | **Direct** — Jokowi-era reform weakened KPK. | `final_evidence` |\n| **S-7B-I6b** *(split, re-typed)* | BTI 2026 Indonesia, §2.4: \"These two regulations, the Undang-Undang Cipta Kerja (Job Creation Laws) and