reedom of Public Information Act. | https://bti-project.org/en/reports/country-report/IDN, \"Freedom of expression\" section | Academic index · medium_high | Cross-period | Indirect | `context` |\n| **R-7B-I11** *(preserved, direct)* | Freedom House 2024 (Jan 2023): \"Jokowi acknowledged 12 major human rights abuses committed by the government, including the 1965–66 massacres, and promised compensation, though he did not offer a formal apology. Papuan activists criticized the government, saying it did not sufficiently acknowledge abuses committed against Papuans.\" | https://freedomhouse.org/country/indonesia/freedom-world/2024, section F4 | NGO · medium_high | Target-year (Jan 2023) | **Direct** | `final_evidence` |\n| **N-7B-3** *(counter-claim — positive correction)* | BBC (23 Nov 2023) coverage of Firli case: \"A corruption conviction for state officials carries a maximum sentence of life in prison.\" Establishes the legal frame in which the dismissal occurred. | https://www.bbc.com/news/world-67509472 | Major public-service media · medium_high | Target-year | Direct (legal frame) | `context` |\n| **N-7B-4** *(contrary — pattern claim)* | The Jakarta Post (23 Nov 2023): \"KPK has prosecuted hundreds of politicians, officials, and businessmen since its formation in 2002, becoming one of the country's most respected agencies.\" | https://www.thejakartapost.com/indonesia/2023/11/23/police-name-kpk-chief-firli-as-suspect-in-alleged-extortion.html | Reputable national media · medium_high | Cross-period | Indirect | `context` (counter-claim on KPK institutional credibility) |\n\n**7B dropped / reclassified:**\n- `IM23-I1` (round 0): **superseded** by R-7B-I1 + N-7B-2 (split out the rule-of-law application).\n- `IM23-I2` (round 0): **superseded** by S-7B-I2a + S-7B-I2b (split into appointment and pattern).\n- `IM23-I3` (round 0): **superseded** by N-7B-1.\n- `IM23-I4` (round 0): **superseded** by R-7B-I4 (re-typed to `context` for ruler attribution; cross-ref 4B).\n- `IM23-I5` (round 0): **superseded** by R-7B-I5 (preserved).\n- `IM23-I6` (round 0): **superseded** by S-7B-I6a (direct) + S-7B-I6b (2019 enactment context).\n- `IM23-I7` (round 0): **superseded** by S-7B-I7a (preserved with attribution).\n- `IM23-I8` (round 0): **superseded** by S-7B-I8a (re-typed to `context` for ruler attribution; institutional, not personal).\n- `IM23-I9` (round 0): **superseded** by S-7B-I9a (rejected — period drift to 2016-17 data).\n- `IM23-I10` (round 0): **superseded** by S-7B-I10a (re-typed to `context`).\n- `IM23-I11` (round 0): **superseded** by R-7B-I11 (preserved).\n\n**Chapter 7B filter ledger (round 1):** 16 source-claim units (under 20-unit ceiling). **7** carry direct executive attribution for 2023 (R-7B-I1, S-7B-I2a, S-7B-I2b, N-7B-1, N-7B-2, R-7B-I5, S-7B-I6a, S-7B-I7a, R-7B-I11 — actually 9). 7 are `context`.\n\n**Lens coverage (round 1):**\n- `7B.1` (truth-telling): R-7B-I11 (partial admission), R-7B-I1 (\"respect the process of law\")\n- `7B.2` (admit error / correct): R-7B-I11, N-7B-1 (dismissal), R-7B-I1\n- `7B.3` (separation of interests): no direct 2023 evidence surfaced\n- `7B.4` (self-enrichment): no direct 2023 evidence surfaced (search note below)\n- `7B.5` (competent appointments): S-7B-I2a (Firli appointment and the KPK-weakening reform), S-7B-I6a\n- `7B.6` (tolerate independent investigation): R-7B-I1 (\"respect the process of law\"), R-7B-I4 (SLAPP — context for ministerial complaint, not ruler)\n- `7B.7` (concealment / obstruction): R-7B-I5 (UU ITE non-signature), R-7B-I4 (SLAPP — context), S-7B-I6a (KPK weakening)\n- `7B.8` (keep promises): R-7B-I11 (admission without apology), R-7B-I5 (UU ITE non-signature), N-7B-3 (life-sentence legal frame)\n- `7B.9` (nepotism / favoritism): S-7B-I8a (honorary doctorates — context)\n- `7B.10` (model ethical standards): S-7B-I7a (Suharto-era continuation frame), N-7B-4 (KPK institutional credibility counter)\n\n**Attribution statement (round 1):** Round 1 establishes that the **Firli Bahuri case** is the most directly attributable 2023 personal-conduct item for Jokowi, because (a) Firli was appointed by Jokowi (2019), (b) the KPK-weakening reform was a Jokowi-era decision, (c) Firli's dismissal in November 2023 was a direct Jokowi action, and (d) Jokowi's \"respect the process of law\" statement is on record. This addresses the reviewer's under-specified accountability chain. The other 7B items remain `context` because they describe institutional or ministerial conduct without direct ruler direction.\n\n**Search limitation note (round 1):** Targeted searches for Jokowi's personal asset declarations, LHKPN filings, family-business conflicts of interest, and procurement decisions did not surface a directly attributable 2023 disclosure event. The Asia Maior honorary-doctorate narrative is institutional, not personal. The \"personal enrichment\" lens therefore remains thin for 2023 specifically; the strongest personal-conduct evidence is the Firli accountability chain.\n\n---\n\n### CHAPTER 8B — Ruler Effectiveness and Competence\n\n**Round-0 estimate:** 6 defensible / 4 families. Reviewer issues: bundled claims, SOE debt attributed without corrective evidence, late election-period evidence mixed with 2023, weak Prabowo lens.\n\n**Round-1 changes:** Split bundled items. Add a direct Jokowi statement on the IKN (from ANTARA). Add a 2023-specific SOE-budget item. Add a counter-claim (N-8B-7) acknowledging that the Whoosh launch and digital-economy growth are visible implementation outcomes. Re-classify BRIN and IKN execution items.\n\n#### 8B retained/restructured items\n\n| ID | Claim | URL / locator | Source type & conf. | Period fit | Ruler attribution evidence | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **S-8B-F1a** *(split)* | EAF (Jan 2024): \"In 2023, Indonesia successfully held the ASEAN chairmanship and hosted the FIFA U-17 World Cup, the first FIFA tournament held in Southeast Asia.\" | https://eastasiaforum.org/2024/01/29/jokowis-final-act/ | Reputable academic-affiliated media · medium_high | Target-year (2023) | Direct (presidential programme) | `final_evidence` |\n| **S-8B-F1b** *(split)* | EAF (Jan 2024): \"Indonesia also launched its first high-speed railway 'Whoosh' connecting Jakarta and Bandung, with a planned extension to Surabaya.\" | Same URL | Reputable academic-affiliated media · medium_high | Target-year (Oct 2023) | Direct (presidential programme) | `final_evidence` |\n| **R-8B-F2** | EAF (Jan 2024): \"SOEs have played a critical role in the success of Jokowi's infrastructure completion, thus contributing to the President's popularity. This reliance on SOEs has expedited projects' implementation. Yet it has caused large financial debts for the SOEs, requiring capital injections from the state budget.\" | https://eastasiaforum.org/2024/01/29/jokowis-final-act/ | Reputable academic-affiliated media · medium_high | Cross-period (covers 2023) | **Direct** (reliance on SOEs is a Jokowi policy choice). | `final_evidence` |\n| **R-8B-F3** | EAF (Jan 2024): \"Jokowi wants to ensure that basic infrastructure will be ready in 2024 when he plans to celebrate Indonesia's anniversary in Nusantara. Nevertheless, private investors (both domestic and foreign) will likely hold off on committing new funding until the next government is confirmed.\" | https://eastasiaforum.org/2024/01/29/jokowis-final-act/ | Reputable academic-affiliated media · medium_high | Target-year (2023) | **Direct** (Jokowi's goal stated; investor caution documented). | `final_evidence` |\n| **S-8B-F4a** *(split)* | Asia Maior Vol XXXV 2024, §1: \"Jokowi's authoritarian turn was functional to the implementation of grand infrastructure development projects, which needed substantial foreign investments.\" | Asia Maior Vol XXXV | Peer-reviewed area-studies journal · medium_high | Cross-period (covers 2023) | **Direct** (programme attribution). | `final_evidence` |\n| **S-8B-F4b** *(split)* | Asia Maior Vol XXXV 2024, §1: \