development.\" | Asia Maior Vol XXXV | Peer-reviewed area-studies journal · medium_high | Cross-period (covers 2023) | Indirect (institutional / military role) | `context` (programme-execution evidence; ecological dimension) |\n| **S-8B-F10a** *(split)* | BTI 2026 Indonesia, summary: \"the quality of democracy in Indonesia continued to decline. The figure bearing primary responsibility for this democratic recession was former President Joko Widodo (often referred to as Jokowi), who sought to extend his political power after serving the two five-year terms allowed by the constitution.\" | https://bti-project.org/en/reports/country-report/IDN, summary | Academic index · medium_high | Cross-period (covers 2023) | **Direct** (democratic-recession framing). | `final_evidence` (cross-ref 4B S-4B-P3a) |\n| **R-8B-F11** | EAF (Jan 2024): \"Healthy domestic consumption is reflected by continued growth in the digital economy, particularly in the e-commerce sector… Finance Minister Sri Mulyani stated that in 2023 Indonesia's digital economy would surge to US$82 billion, marking an 8 per cent increase from 2022.\" | https://eastasiaforum.org/2024/01/29/jokowis-final-act/ | Reputable academic-affiliated media · medium_high | Target-year (2023) | Direct (minister's statement on executive programme) | `context` |\n| **N-8B-4** | EAF (Jan 2024): \"While spending on infrastructure is needed to support growth, the government must implement a robust cost-benefit analysis before implementing any infrastructure projects. Arguably, state-owned enterprises (SOEs) have played a critical role in the success of Jokowi's infrastructure completion, thus contributing to the President's popularity.\" | https://eastasiaforum.org/2024/01/29/jokowis-final-act/ | Reputable academic-affiliated media · medium_high | Cross-period (covers 2023) | **Direct** | `final_evidence` (implementation-attribute lens) |\n| **N-8B-5** | EAF (Jan 2024): \"this reliance on SOEs has expedited projects' implementation. Yet it has caused large financial debts for the SOEs, requiring capital injections from the state budget.\" | https://eastasiaforum.org/2024/01/29/jokowis-final-act/ | Reputable academic-affiliated media · medium_high | Cross-period (covers 2023) | **Direct** (capital-injection requirement attributable to Jokowi's SOE-reliance programme). | `final_evidence` (corrective-responsibility lens) |\n| **N-8B-6** | EAF (Jan 2024): \"the government responded with price stabilisation policies and social assistance to protect the purchasing power of the poor and vulnerable. Social assistance policies included an additional 2.7 trillion Indonesian rupiah (US$173.2 million) in food assistance and 7.5 trillion rupiah (US$481.5 million) in direct cash assistance to poor households.\" | https://eastasiaforum.org/2024/01/29/jokowis-final-act/ | Reputable academic-affiliated media · medium_high | Target-year (2023) | **Direct** (government response). | `final_evidence` (cross-ref 5B S-5B-E1b, 6B S-6B-S1a) |\n| **N-8B-7** *(counter-claim — implementation positive)* | EAF (Jan 2024): \"The COVID-19 pandemic has accelerated the adoption of digital technologies and online commerce. Consumer preference for online shopping remains persistent after the COVID-19 pandemic.\" | https://eastasiaforum.org/2024/01/29/jokowis-final-act/ | Reputable academic-affiliated media · medium_high | Cross-period | Indirect | `context` (counter-claim: digital-economy momentum survived transition) |\n| **N-8B-8** | The Diplomat (14 Dec 2023): \"The future of Indonesia's new capital stands as one of the pivotal policy questions ahead of the upcoming 2024 elections in Indonesia. Launched during President Joko 'Jokowi' Widodo's administration, this ambitious megaplan seeks to create Nusantara, a new capital city, from scratch on the island of Borneo, at a cost of 466 trillion rupiah (nearly $30 billion) by 2045… 'IKN already operates under the constitution; our objective is not to centralize Indonesia around Ja